      "math_academy_id": "q-80482",
      "sequence_position": 13,
      "problem": "Given that $C$ and $D$ are finite, non-overlapping regions and that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{C}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=7,\\,{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=1,\n$$\n\nfind the value of \n\n$$\n{∬}_{C\\cup D}5f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the linearity and additivity of double integrals, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{C\\cup D}5f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =5{∬}_{C\\cup D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A \\\\  & =5({∬}_{C}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A+{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A) \\\\  & =5(7+1) \\\\  & =40\\end{aligned}\n$$",
